# The one thing this app needs: a Convex deployment of your own. Uncomment the
# line below, paste your deployment URL over the example, save — the dev server
# watches this file, so the page turns from its setup panel into the live demo
# with nothing to restart.
#
#   https://dashboard.convex.dev → your project → Settings → Deployment URL
#
# Or run `npm run convex` and let the Convex CLI write the line for you.

# CONVEX_URL=https://your-deployment.convex.cloud

# Why commented rather than left empty to fill in: a variable that is *defined
# but empty* when the dev server starts stays empty for the life of that
# process — dotenv will not overwrite a variable that already exists — so
# filling it in afterwards would quietly do nothing until you restarted. An
# absent variable is picked up on the next restart, which the watcher does for
# you. Same reason the name here is unprefixed; see `nuxt.config.ts`.
#
# This file is committed, because it ships with the StackBlitz sandbox. What
# you and the Convex CLI add to it is yours — check `git diff` before you
# commit it back.
